  "policies": [
    "Constable selects each physical Imp-formant in the opponent current deck with one weight; empty pool has no RNG, a singleton ordinary random selection still consumes RNG. Reordering preserves other relative order, zone residence and attachments; then buffs only the original selected stored reference. This is placement, not a shuffle.",
    "Mastermind installs independent persistent player instances. Each original successful friendly Imp-formant entry receives its2/2 via a bounded original summon ID and continuous board residence, not current name or reused entity ID. Same-residence face/control changes retain the accepted receiver; death/return/reentry do not rebind.",
    "Source silence/death/control does not remove the player instance. New sources and genuine repeated Battlecries stack normally. Initial Scenario bodies and failed summons are not actual successful entries.",
    "Both public additions reuse original deck reorder/stored buff and current board buff handlers; no new state fields, counters, schedulers or invented combinations. Exact CN random/top/buff/notification/transform/control windows remain uncalibrated."
  ]
